  "name": "Notes on the Body Mass of Pinnipeds in the Eastern Bering Sea Based on Life Table Data",
  "description": "Uniform format life talbes for seven pinniped species were prepared using previously published data on body mass and natural mortality rates by age. These data were pooled by sex, and a single point estimate of the average body mass for the population was calculated from the life table data. Pinniped species include northern fur seal (Callorhinus ursinus), northern sea lions (Eumetopias jubatus), Pacific harbor seals (Phoca vitulina richardii), spotted seals (Phoca largha), ringed seals (Phoca hispida), ribbon seals (Phoca fasciata), and bearded seals (Erignathus barbatus) in the Bering Sea. [Reference: McAlister, B. Notes on the Body Mass of Pinnipeds in the Eastern Bering Sea Based on Life Table Data. Dec. 1987. 21 p.] Unpublished report available at the NOAA NMML Library.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Notes on the Body Mass of Pinnipeds in the Eastern Bering Sea Based on life Table data.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563655",
